  "body": "Stacked on #2974. Review the [placed DXF wire changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/760e62cc194f49d6efb51cfd557574d7df4cede0...80daeae0852e3f46a6ebfa5b47c13aeb2689b592).\n\nUse one closed DXF racetrack or circle as the source for a vertical punch. Keep the original lines and arcs through placement, normal Wire Contour generation, verification and native output. Invalidate the toolpath when the source or placement changes. The conservative preview encloses the exact arcs with at most 0.000025 mm of radial excess.\n\nA racetrack needs two parallel cardinal straight sides tangent to two semicircles. A circle needs a radius from 6 through 15 mm and a radial threading lead on a cardinal side. The native grid must represent the circle and the intended seam. Individual chain selection, other drawings and laser work remain part of #2022.\n\nRun the original examples from the repository root:\n\n```sh\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/racetrack.camscript\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/circle-punch.camscript\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/north-circle.camscript\n```\n\nThe translated and 90 degree rotated R10 racetrack generated 1,409 moves with zero warnings. Agie Control kept the arc centers at (−6, 1) and (10, 1). It reported pass radii of 10.245, 10.155, 10.140 and 10.134 mm. The arc direction reversed on alternate passes. The separation on the straight section measured 1.000 mm.\n\nOn circular jobs, each bridge swept 1/R radians for a 1.000 mm nominal arc. The rough and trim wire paths stayed concentric. Three CAMCraft jobs exercised R6 east, R10 west and R15 north. Separate synthetic reference jobs checked all four cardinal directions at R10. The formal checks reported zero job errors. The control requested machining and reference setup and reported option 131072. No physical cut was made.\n\nThe independent gate passed 24 scoped app tests, 15 native post tests and both round-profile geometry tests. Strict Clippy passed for the app, geometry and post libraries. In the integrated feature branch, all 13 example jobs and three additional stock heights exported correctly. All 50 files matched their earlier verified output. Each repeat export preserved every file.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Placed DXF racetracks and circles can drive a verified Wire Contour punch and produce native Agie arcs from the original drawing.\n\nRefs #2022\n",
